//github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dzajenckauskas/toolkit/commits/b20e399e3f1083a56b1cbe18e427270c1f5b60ce/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-12T18:22:08Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-12T18:22:08Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Update CHANGELOG for the catalog quick-wins batch\n\nRecords #33, #34, #35, #36, #39, #40, #41 under Unreleased.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PizcP83WdmFR8APtR9z9JS","tree":{"sha":"614042bc5d6e8d457c1ee78ca85f87f92081cb47","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dzajenckauskas/toolkit/git/trees/614042bc5d6e8d457c1ee78ca85f87f92081cb47"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dzajenckauskas/toolkit/git/commits/b20e399e3f1083a56b1cbe18e427270c1f5b60ce","verification":{"payload":"tree 614042bc5d6e8d457c1ee78ca85f87f92081cb47\nparent 053412b369f9e543e78636aa68d5d5e0ae7c1b8e\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1786558928 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1786558928 +0000\n\nUpdate CHANGELOG for the catalog quick-wins batch\n\nRecords #33, #34, #35, #36, #39, #40, #41 under Unreleased.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PizcP83WdmFR8APtR9z9JS\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQBx5I/JY\nWDBYSOHnXb2zL/BH7Y5+Vn7ndD+AkUKXIRm61rv4QKuk5DPPPmDiMTXWCkdZCs8f6/CprzJkR3zI\nPgI=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-12T18:27:14Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/dzajenckauskas/toolkit/commit/b20e399e3f1083a56b1cbe18e427270c1f5b60ce","node_id":"C_kwDOThO8otoAKGIyMGUzOTllM2YxMDgzYTU2YjFjYmUxOGU0MjcyNzBjMWY1YjYwY2U","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dzajenckauskas/toolkit/commit/053412b369f9e543e78636aa68d5d5e0ae7c1b8e","sha":"053412b369f9e543e78636aa68d5d5e0ae7c1b8e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dzajenckauskas/toolkit/commits/053412b369f9e543e78636aa68d5d5e0ae7c1b8e"}],"sha":"b20e399e3f1083a56b1cbe18e427270c1f5b60ce","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dzajenckauskas/toolkit/commits/b20e399e3f1083a56b1cbe18e427270c1f5b60ce"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dzajenckauskas/toolkit/commits/053412b369f9e543e78636aa68d5d5e0ae7c1b8e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-12T18:17:50Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-12T18:17:50Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Accept all image formats in Crop and Optimize (#33)\n\nCrop and Optimize were hardcoded to JPEG-only input via the Sprint-001\n`validateFile`/`ACCEPTED_MIME_TYPES` constants, rejecting PNG/WebP even\nthough every other image tool already accepts them. Bring both onto the\nshared broad-format path and preserve the source format on output.\n\nLib (image.ts):\n- `imageFormatForInput(type, name)` — preserve JPEG/PNG/WebP; GIF/BMP and\n  unknowns fall back to lossless PNG (canvas can decode but not encode\n  them). Pure, unit-tested.\n- `optimizeImage(input, format, quality)` — format-aware, same-size\n  re-encode with the transparency-safe background fill; quality only\n  applies to lossy formats. Replaces the JPEG-only `optimizeJpeg`.\n\nOptimizer:\n- Accepts JPG/PNG/WebP (picker + drag-and-drop + paste) via\n  `validateImageFile`; preserves the input format on output and names the\n  download by the real output extension. The compression control is\n  disabled with a note for a lossless (PNG-only) batch, since quality\n  doesn''t apply.\n\nCropper:\n- Same broad acceptance; the download re-encodes in the source format\n  (transparent PNGs stay PNG, no forced-JPEG black fill) with the correct\n  extension. Copy no longer says \"JPEG\".\n\nCleanup: removed the now-dead JPEG-only plumbing — `validation.ts`\n(`validateFile`) and its test, `filename.ts` (`generateOutputFilename`,\nsuperseded by `outputImageName`) and its test, and the\n`ACCEPTED_MIME_TYPES`/`ACCEPTED_EXTENSIONS`/`OUTPUT_SUFFIX` constants;\nretired the unused `encodeJpeg`/`optimizeJpeg` from optimize.ts and fixed\na stale clipboard comment.\n\nTests: unit for `imageFormatForInput`; e2e for a PNG through Crop\n(preserves .png) and Optimize (preserves .png, lossless control\ndisabled). Existing JPEG behavior unchanged. Full suite green (252 unit,\n103 e2e).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PizcP83WdmFR8APtR9z9JS","tree":{"sha":"8ab5dc2838d6119f10b8bc5dd98e143201ff0a22","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dzajenckauskas/toolkit/git/trees/8ab5dc2838d6119f10b8bc5dd98e143201ff0a22"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dzajenckauskas/toolkit/git/commits/053412b369f9e543e78636aa68d5d5e0ae7c1b8e","verification":{"payload":"tree 8ab5dc2838d6119f10b8bc5dd98e143201ff0a22\nparent 3bc9b9e091ba1c57bcb8bbd39edc01ea1f85d1f4\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1786558670 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1786558670 +0000\n\nAccept all image formats in Crop and Optimize (#33)\n\nCrop and Optimize were hardcoded to JPEG-only input via the Sprint-001\n`validateFile`/`ACCEPTED_MIME_TYPES` constants, rejecting PNG/WebP even\nthough every other image tool already accepts them. Bring both onto the\nshared broad-format path and preserve the source format on output.\n\nLib (image.ts):\n- `imageFormatForInput(type, name)` — preserve JPEG/PNG/WebP; GIF/BMP and\n  unknowns fall back to lossless PNG (canvas can decode but not encode\n  them). Pure, unit-tested.\n- `optimizeImage(input, format, quality)` — format-aware, same-size\n  re-encode with the transparency-safe background fill; quality only\n  applies to lossy formats. Replaces the JPEG-only `optimizeJpeg`.\n\nOptimizer:\n- Accepts JPG/PNG/WebP (picker + drag-and-drop + paste) via\n  `validateImageFile`; preserves the input format on output and names the\n  download by the real output extension. The compression control is\n  disabled with a note for a lossless (PNG-only) batch, since quality\n  doesn''t apply.\n\nCropper:\n- Same broad acceptance; the download re-encodes in the source format\n  (transparent PNGs stay PNG, no forced-JPEG black fill) with the correct\n  extension. Copy no longer says \"JPEG\".\n\nCleanup: removed the now-dead JPEG-only plumbing — `validation.ts`\n(`validateFile`) and its test, `filename.ts` (`generateOutputFilename`,\nsuperseded by `outputImageName`) and its test, and the\n`ACCEPTED_MIME_TYPES`/`ACCEPTED_EXTENSIONS`/`OUTPUT_SUFFIX` constants;\nretired the unused `encodeJpeg`/`optimizeJpeg` from optimize.ts and fixed\na stale clipboard comment.\n\nTests: unit for `imageFormatForInput`; e2e for a PNG through Crop\n(preserves .png) and Optimize (preserves .png, lossless control\ndisabled). Existing JPEG behavior unchanged. Full suite green (252 unit,\n103 e2e).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PizcP83WdmFR8APtR9z9JS\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQL3t4AnP\njcQXt0D/dNxEtcwLyCuY4/T2RrGq1ieziZheIRvcbq6BjYxLSYAM/jOgiOHKMGuH3UQMIIu/HgiM\nYAA=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-12T18:19:44Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/dzajenckauskas/toolkit/commit/053412b369f9e543e78636aa68d5d5e0ae7c1b8e","node_id":"C_kwDOThO8otoAKDA1MzQxMmIzNjlmOWU1NDNlNzg2MzZhYTY4ZDVkNWUwYWU3YzFiOGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dzajenckauskas/toolkit/commit/3bc9b9e091ba1c57bcb8bbd39edc01ea1f85d1f4","sha":"3bc9b9e091ba1c57bcb8bbd39edc01ea1f85d1f4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dzajenckauskas/toolkit/commits/3bc9b9e091ba1c57bcb8bbd39edc01ea1f85d1f4"}],"sha":"053412b369f9e543e78636aa68d5d5e0ae7c1b8e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dzajenckauskas/toolkit/commits/053412b369f9e543e78636aa68d5d5e0ae7c1b8e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dzajenckauskas/toolkit/commits/3bc9b9e091ba1c57bcb8bbd39edc01ea1f85d1f4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-12T18:01:17Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-12T18:01:17Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Add marketplace crop presets to the Cropper (#35)\n\nAdds a \"Marketplace preset\" picker alongside the existing free\naspect-ratio and export-size options. Each preset locks both the crop\nbox''s aspect ratio and an exact output pixel size — distinct from the\nfree options, which only fix a shape and a longest edge.\n\n- packages/lib/src/crop.ts: MARKETPLACE_PRESETS (Amazon 2000², Etsy\n  2700×2025, eBay 1600², Shopify 2048², Instagram 1080² and 1080×1350),\n  `presetRatio`, and `resolveOutputSize` — a preset forces its exact\n  size, otherwise the crop scales to the longest edge as before.\n- Cropper.tsx: preset radio group; selecting one locks the box to the\n  preset ratio and disables the now-superseded aspect-ratio/export-size\n  fieldsets; \"None\" hands control back. Output display and download both\n  honor the exact preset size.\n- Unit tests for the preset→ratio and preset→output-size mapping; e2e for\n  selecting a preset, the forced exact size, the disabled controls, and\n  clearing back to free.\n- ROADMAP: Cropper \"Ecommerce presets\" checked off.\n\nAdditive — existing free-crop, aspect-ratio, export-size and zoom\nbehavior unchanged.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PizcP83WdmFR8APtR9z9JS","tree":{"sha":"2561ad23b6f11e0bace9f3676428e139ad16310f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dzajenckauskas/toolkit/git/trees/2561ad23b6f11e0bace9f3676428e139ad16310f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dzajenckauskas/toolkit/git/commits/3bc9b9e091ba1c57bcb8bbd39edc01ea1f85d1f4","verification":{"payload":"tree 2561ad23b6f11e0bace9f3676428e139ad16310f\nparent 36843f3a0f9b9e640cc701f326880441432d14b7\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1786557677 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1786557677 +0000\n\nAdd marketplace crop presets to the Cropper (#35)\n\nAdds a \"Marketplace preset\" picker alongside the existing free\naspect-ratio and export-size options. Each preset locks both the crop\nbox''s aspect ratio and an exact output pixel size — distinct from the\nfree options, which only fix a shape and a longest edge.\n\n- packages/lib/src/crop.ts: MARKETPLACE_PRESETS (Amazon 2000², Etsy\n  2700×2025, eBay 1600², Shopify 2048², Instagram 1080² and 1080×1350),\n  `presetRatio`, and `resolveOutputSize` — a preset forces its exact\n  size, otherwise the crop scales to the longest edge as before.\n- Cropper.tsx: preset radio group; selecting one locks the box to the\n  preset ratio and disables the now-superseded aspect-ratio/export-size\n  fieldsets; \"None\" hands control back. Output display and download both\n  honor the exact preset size.\n- Unit tests for the preset→ratio and preset→output-size mapping; e2e for\n  selecting a preset, the forced exact size, the disabled controls, and\n  clearing back to free.\n- ROADMAP: Cropper \"Ecommerce presets\" checked off.\n\nAdditive — existing free-crop, aspect-ratio, export-size and zoom\nbehavior unchanged.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PizcP83WdmFR8APtR9z9JS\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQGrEgcvf\nhj7xP1Z6pFweLeLZPCmp3YbG9SwX9wA2ZRsM3+AtStnVPeX14jwjREq0U3vQrzZbOFUBb7y1m2yi\n4gQ=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-12T18:02:43Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/dzajenckauskas/toolkit/commit/3bc9b9e091ba1c57bcb8bbd39edc01ea1f85d1f4","node_id":"C_kwDOThO8otoAKDNiYzliOWUwOTFiYTFjNTdiY2I4YmJkMzllZGMwMWVhMWY4NWQxZjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dzajenckauskas/toolkit/commit/36843f3a0f9b9e640cc701f326880441432d14b7","sha":"36843f3a0f9b9e640cc701f326880441432d14b7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dzajenckauskas/toolkit/commits/36843f3a0f9b9e640cc701f326880441432d14b7"}],"sha":"3bc9b9e091ba1c57bcb8bbd39edc01ea1f85d1f4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dzajenckauskas/toolkit/commits/3bc9b9e091ba1c57bcb8bbd39edc01ea1f85d1f4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dzajenckauskas/toolkit/commits/36843f3a0f9b9e640cc701f326880441432d14b7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-12T17:54:22Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-12T17:54:22Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Add a JWT generator (encoder) alongside the decoder (#41)\n\nThe JWT tool was decode-only. Add HMAC signing so it pairs an encoder\nwith the decoder, like jwt.io.\n\n- packages/lib/src/jwt.ts: pure `encodeJwt(header, payload, secret, alg)`\n  symmetric with `decodeJwt`, signing HS256/HS384/HS512 via Web Crypto\n  (reusing the webcrypto helpers). The header `alg` is forced to the\n  algorithm actually used, so a token can''t claim one algorithm while\n  signed with another. Round-trips with `decodeJwt`.\n- JwtGenerator.tsx: JSON header/payload editors, secret, algorithm\n  select, live-signed token with copy and download — consistent with the\n  other developer tools. JwtTool.tsx adds a Decode/Generate toggle over\n  the existing decoder (Decode stays the default).\n- Unit tests: canonical jwt.io known-answer token, decode round-trip,\n  alg-can''t-be-spoofed, per-algorithm signatures. Browser test covers\n  generate → download → decode round-trip and the invalid-JSON error.\n- Registry: JWT description + keywords now mention encode/sign/generate.\n\nClient-side HMAC only (matches the no-backend model); RS256/asymmetric\nis out of scope.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PizcP83WdmFR8APtR9z9JS","tree":{"sha":"306fff80a361e2424e5bd90159716db6618c4ca4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dzajenckauskas/toolkit/git/trees/306fff80a361e2424e5bd90159716db6618c4ca4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dzajenckauskas/toolkit/git/commits/36843f3a0f9b9e640cc701f326880441432d14b7","verification":{"payload":"tree 306fff80a361e2424e5bd90159716db6618c4ca4\nparent 04ec7ce3b6b89aa934ee3b21fa3f4dcac6342ba0\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1786557262 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1786557262 +0000\n\nAdd a JWT generator (encoder) alongside the decoder (#41)\n\nThe JWT tool was decode-only. Add HMAC signing so it pairs an encoder\nwith the decoder, like jwt.io.\n\n- packages/lib/src/jwt.ts: pure `encodeJwt(header, payload, secret, alg)`\n  symmetric with `decodeJwt`, signing HS256/HS384/HS512 via Web Crypto\n  (reusing the webcrypto helpers). The header `alg` is forced to the\n  algorithm actually used, so a token can''t claim one algorithm while\n  signed with another. Round-trips with `decodeJwt`.\n- JwtGenerator.tsx: JSON header/payload editors, secret, algorithm\n  select, live-signed token with copy and download — consistent with the\n  other developer tools. JwtTool.tsx adds a Decode/Generate toggle over\n  the existing decoder (Decode stays the default).\n- Unit tests: canonical jwt.io known-answer token, decode round-trip,\n  alg-can''t-be-spoofed, per-algorithm signatures. Browser test covers\n  generate → download → decode round-trip and the invalid-JSON error.\n- Registry: JWT description + keywords now mention encode/sign/generate.\n\nClient-side HMAC only (matches the no-backend model); RS256/asymmetric\nis out of scope.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PizcP83WdmFR8APtR9z9JS\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJsQ9QDJ\nVqXqIRqjqNf/UbVkZ7app40trb1k0pyYXNnO6Eea6rQxNdTVWcc+mtMltZS7/cTJCcNXUaFPCNox\n3ws=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-12T17:59:26Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/dzajenckauskas/toolkit/commit/36843f3a0f9b9e640cc701f326880441432d14b7","node_id":"C_kwDOThO8otoAKDM2ODQzZjNhMGY5YjllNjQwY2M3MDFmMzI2ODgwNDQxNDMyZDE0Yjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dzajenckauskas/toolkit/commit/04ec7ce3b6b89aa934ee3b21fa3f4dcac6342ba0","sha":"04ec7ce3b6b89aa934ee3b21fa3f4dcac6342ba0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dzajenckauskas/toolkit/commits/04ec7ce3b6b89aa934ee3b21fa3f4dcac6342ba0"}],"sha":"36843f3a0f9b9e640cc701f326880441432d14b7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dzajenckauskas/toolkit/commits/36843f3a0f9b9e640cc701f326880441432d14b7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dzajenckauskas/toolkit/commits/04ec7ce3b6b89aa934ee3b21fa3f4dcac6342ba0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-12T17:47:24Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-12T17:47:24Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Add styled 404 and error boundary for tool routes (#39)\n\nThe app had no App Router not-found/error boundaries, so an unknown or\nrenamed route fell back to Next.js''s bare default 404 and an uncaught\nrender error inside a tool showed a blank/default page — both off-brand.\n\n- app/not-found.tsx: styled 404 rendered inside the root layout (header +\n  footer), with a \"Back to all tools\" link to the catalog. Marked\n  noindex.\n- app/error.tsx: client error boundary that catches an uncaught render\n  error in any tool page and shows a styled recovery screen with \"Try\n  again\" (reset) and a catalog link, instead of a blank page.\n\nBoth use the design-system primitives. e2e covers the 404 case: an\nunknown route returns 404, renders the styled page in the app shell, and\nits catalog link recovers.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PizcP83WdmFR8APtR9z9JS","tree":{"sha":"c66dc70306928a70ed6051dc3b5115d4c723d992","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dzajenckauskas/toolkit/git/trees/c66dc70306928a70ed6051dc3b5115d4c723d992"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dzajenckauskas/toolkit/git/commits/04ec7ce3b6b89aa934ee3b21fa3f4dcac6342ba0","verification":{"payload":"tree c66dc70306928a70ed6051dc3b5115d4c723d992\nparent 74493cdce74f6f81d0ffb5c753f0f52ab505397c\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1786556844 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1786556844 +0000\n\nAdd styled 404 and error boundary for tool routes (#39)\n\nThe app had no App Router not-found/error boundaries, so an unknown or\nrenamed route fell back to Next.js''s bare default 404 and an uncaught\nrender error inside a tool showed a blank/default page — both off-brand.\n\n- app/not-found.tsx: styled 404 rendered inside the root layout (header +\n  footer), with a \"Back to all tools\" link to the catalog. Marked\n  noindex.\n- app/error.tsx: client error boundary that catches an uncaught render\n  error in any tool page and shows a styled recovery screen with \"Try\n  again\" (reset) and a catalog link, instead of a blank page.\n\nBoth use the design-system primitives. e2e covers the 404 case: an\nunknown route returns 404, renders the styled page in the app shell, and\nits catalog link recovers.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PizcP83WdmFR8APtR9z9JS\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQKvnwQWW\nTDVsv0c61O/AXzFagUsABqArSy3V2SZfyHl4d3mzjuaXvBJFCKmpAWtlZh3u/dOhodz30nlA02eO\neQw=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-12T17:52:27Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/dzajenckauskas/toolkit/commit/04ec7ce3b6b89aa934ee3b21fa3f4dcac6342ba0","node_id":"C_kwDOThO8otoAKDA0ZWM3Y2UzYjZiODlhYTkzNGVlM2IyMWZhM2Y0ZGNhYzYzNDJiYTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dzajenckauskas/toolkit/commit/74493cdce74f6f81d0ffb5c753f0f52ab505397c","sha":"74493cdce74f6f81d0ffb5c753f0f52ab505397c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dzajenckauskas/toolkit/commits/74493cdce74f6f81d0ffb5c753f0f52ab505397c"}],"sha":"04ec7ce3b6b89aa934ee3b21fa3f4dcac6342ba0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dzajenckauskas/toolkit/commits/04ec7ce3b6b89aa934ee3b21fa3f4dcac6342ba0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dzajenckauskas/toolkit/commits/74493cdce74f6f81d0ffb5c753f0f52ab505397c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-12T17:41:47Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-12T17:41:47Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Add Soon / New / Top card badges to the catalog (#40)\n\nReplace the single \"Soon\" chip with a three-tier badge system, resolved\nby one `toolBadge()` helper in the registry (precedence: soon > new > top):\n\n- Soon — planned tools (unchanged behaviour, grey outline).\n- New  — a live tool within NEW_TOOL_WINDOW_DAYS (30) of its `addedAt`\n  launch date. Date-driven so it appears and expires on its own with no\n  manual cleanup. Flagged: accessibility-checker (2026-08-10),\n  screenshot (2026-07-28).\n- Top  — a curated `featured: true` flagship; never expires. Flagged:\n  image editor, compress, QR code, JSON, colors.\n\nA shared ToolBadge component renders the badge (filled accent for New,\naccent-tinted outline for Top, grey for Soon) on both catalog cards and\nsearch rows, replacing the duplicated Soon chips. Registry unit tests\ncover isNewTool''s window boundaries and toolBadge precedence; a\ntime-robust e2e computes expected badges from the registry so it stays\nhonest as launch windows expire. Recipe in PROJECT-STATE documents how to\nflag a tool.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PizcP83WdmFR8APtR9z9JS","tree":{"sha":"58ddb5830a7948d1d11d1cdf8af92656b9f4b8bd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dzajenckauskas/toolkit/git/trees/58ddb5830a7948d1d11d1cdf8af92656b9f4b8bd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dzajenckauskas/toolkit/git/commits/74493cdce74f6f81d0ffb5c753f0f52ab505397c","verification":{"payload":"tree 58ddb5830a7948d1d11d1cdf8af92656b9f4b8bd\nparent a7829a04e03543eff15ff1cf0105b39e99a8bc97\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1786556507 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1786556507 +0000\n\nAdd Soon / New / Top card badges to the catalog (#40)\n\nReplace the single \"Soon\" chip with a three-tier badge system, resolved\nby one `toolBadge()` helper in the registry (precedence: soon > new > top):\n\n- Soon — planned tools (unchanged behaviour, grey outline).\n- New  — a live tool within NEW_TOOL_WINDOW_DAYS (30) of its `addedAt`\n  launch date. Date-driven so it appears and expires on its own with no\n  manual cleanup. Flagged: accessibility-checker (2026-08-10),\n  screenshot (2026-07-28).\n- Top  — a curated `featured: true` flagship; never expires. Flagged:\n  image editor, compress, QR code, JSON, colors.\n\nA shared ToolBadge component renders the badge (filled accent for New,\naccent-tinted outline for Top, grey for Soon) on both catalog cards and\nsearch rows, replacing the duplicated Soon chips. Registry unit tests\ncover isNewTool''s window boundaries and toolBadge precedence; a\ntime-robust e2e computes expected badges from the registry so it stays\nhonest as launch windows expire. Recipe in PROJECT-STATE documents how to\nflag a tool.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PizcP83WdmFR8APtR9z9JS\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAA