to\npackage.json. Committing keeps the two in agreement — npm ci fails outright\nwhen the lockfile drifts from the manifest.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01APBjHWUcg9exofbWm48XK1","tree":{"sha":"d0aceb23c479cf3a251d37ea69e874eb4e840660","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Hardthrone1/Vega-Midas-Lite-Quant-Tower/git/trees/d0aceb23c479cf3a251d37ea69e874eb4e840660"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Hardthrone1/Vega-Midas-Lite-Quant-Tower/git/commits/c70bca4daa5d0ab2e1141b9c4801ca8d7f15c303","verification":{"payload":"tree d0aceb23c479cf3a251d37ea69e874eb4e840660\nparent b44131192c7bad5f8caa5172dd78d5cb7d8a8a60\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1785094945 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1785094945 +0000\n\nchore(deploy): sync package-lock with engines field\n\nnpm install regenerated the lockfile after engines node>=20 was added to\npackage.json. Committing keeps the two in agreement — npm ci fails outright\nwhen the lockfile drifts from the manifest.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01APBjHWUcg9exofbWm48XK1\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQIQ1b8nx\n2GLFBNoyl0jI05Di5+i8fvMSJy7p6Hew/1ZPXPuB3hvk9U5EhXho/cvmAJaTeJUL8bTlUJ/qBYI0\nJwA=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-26T19:42:27Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Hardthrone1/Vega-Midas-Lite-Quant-Tower/commit/c70bca4daa5d0ab2e1141b9c4801ca8d7f15c303","node_id":"C_kwDOTiNWD9oAKGM3MGJjYTRkYWE1ZDBhYjJlMTE0MWI5YzQ4MDFjYThkN2YxNWMzMDM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Hardthrone1/Vega-Midas-Lite-Quant-Tower/commit/b44131192c7bad5f8caa5172dd78d5cb7d8a8a60","sha":"b44131192c7bad5f8caa5172dd78d5cb7d8a8a60","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Hardthrone1/Vega-Midas-Lite-Quant-Tower/commits/b44131192c7bad5f8caa5172dd78d5cb7d8a8a60"}],"sha":"c70bca4daa5d0ab2e1141b9c4801ca8d7f15c303","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Hardthrone1/Vega-Midas-Lite-Quant-Tower/commits/c70bca4daa5d0ab2e1141b9c4801ca8d7f15c303"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Hardthrone1/Vega-Midas-Lite-Quant-Tower/commits/b44131192c7bad5f8caa5172dd78d5cb7d8a8a60/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-26T19:41:42Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-26T19:41:42Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"feat(deploy): make the tower deployable on Railway as one service\n\nThe gateway crash-looped on Railway for reasons that all had to be fixed\nbefore any deploy could work:\n\n- app.listen bound ''127.0.0.1'' — loopback is unreachable from outside the\n  container, so the platform health check failed and restarted it forever.\n  Now binds 0.0.0.0 when RAILWAY_ENVIRONMENT is set, loopback locally.\n- PORT was hardcoded 8001; Railway assigns a random $PORT. Now reads env.\n- Root package.json had no start or build script (only a `test` that ran\n  `exit 1`), and there was no railway.json/Procfile, so nothing valid could\n  launch. Added both, plus engines node>=20.\n- .nixpacksignore keeps the builder from treating this as a Python project\n  (the MRE server and quant skills are local-only tools).\n- Build skips the electron binary that react-devtools pulls in.\n\nArchitecture: one service. The gateway now serves midas_code/dist as static\nfiles with an SPA fallback, so the API and dashboard share an origin and no\nCORS config is needed. Vite is a build step, not a third server.\n\nSecurity: /api/* now requires an X-Vega-Key header matching VEGA_API_KEY\n(timing-safe compare; /api/health exempt so platform probes pass; no-op when\nunset for local dev). Without this a public URL would let anyone spend the\n~20 provider keys the gateway holds — CORS does not stop curl.\n\nFrontend: new shared/gateway.ts is the single source of truth for the API\nbase. SwarmPanel and AgentConsole had hardcoded http://127.0.0.1:8001, which\nwould have called the visitor''s own machine from a deployed page. All three\ncall sites now use gatewayFetch(), which resolves same-origin in production\nbuilds and attaches the shared secret.\n\nVerified end to end against a simulated deploy (PORT=4567,\nRAILWAY_ENVIRONMENT set): boots on 0.0.0.0, health 200 without a key, API 401\nwithout/with wrong key and reaches the handler with the right one, dashboard\nroot, SPA deep link, and hashed assets all 200.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01APBjHWUcg9exofbWm48XK1","tree":{"sha":"727c41ef366da9441c2e5dbf6b0e55aa408dce50","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Hardthrone1/Vega-Midas-Lite-Quant-Tower/git/trees/727c41ef366da9441c2e5dbf6b0e55aa408dce50"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Hardthrone1/Vega-Midas-Lite-Quant-Tower/git/commits/b44131192c7bad5f8caa5172dd78d5cb7d8a8a60","verification":{"payload":"tree 727c41ef366da9441c2e5dbf6b0e55aa408dce50\nparent aadd5f6e39604f5e7bd636f04cb73b7613cfe780\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1785094902 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1785094902 +0000\n\nfeat(deploy): make the tower deployable on Railway as one service\n\nThe gateway crash-looped on Railway for reasons that all had to be fixed\nbefore any deploy could work:\n\n- app.listen bound ''127.0.0.1'' — loopback is unreachable from outside the\n  container, so the platform health check failed and restarted it forever.\n  Now binds 0.0.0.0 when RAILWAY_ENVIRONMENT is set, loopback locally.\n- PORT was hardcoded 8001; Railway assigns a random $PORT. Now reads env.\n- Root package.json had no start or build script (only a `test` that ran\n  `exit 1`), and there was no railway.json/Procfile, so nothing valid could\n  launch. Added both, plus engines node>=20.\n- .nixpacksignore keeps the builder from treating this as a Python project\n  (the MRE server and quant skills are local-only tools).\n- Build skips the electron binary that react-devtools pulls in.\n\nArchitecture: one service. The gateway now serves midas_code/dist as static\nfiles with an SPA fallback, so the API and dashboard share an origin and no\nCORS config is needed. Vite is a build step, not a third server.\n\nSecurity: /api/* now requires an X-Vega-Key header matching VEGA_API_KEY\n(timing-safe compare; /api/health exempt so platform probes pass; no-op when\nunset for local dev). Without this a public URL would let anyone spend the\n~20 provider keys the gateway holds — CORS does not stop curl.\n\nFrontend: new shared/gateway.ts is the single source of truth for the API\nbase. SwarmPanel and AgentConsole had hardcoded http://127.0.0.1:8001, which\nwould have called the visitor''s own machine from a deployed page. All three\ncall sites now use gatewayFetch(), which resolves same-origin in production\nbuilds and attaches the shared secret.\n\nVerified end to end against a simulated deploy (PORT=4567,\nRAILWAY_ENVIRONMENT set): boots on 0.0.0.0, health 200 without a key, API 401\nwithout/with wrong key and reaches the handler with the right one, dashboard\nroot, SPA deep link, and hashed assets all 200.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01APBjHWUcg9exofbWm48XK1\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQGRu8e8K\nBjociqZwcuZn02oCHoQEQUdVIya7xdPwZpNcM+zv4oMByw+SlDPaJIpV6QA7C23TAm54tizn08DG\nRAE=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-26T19:41:44Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Hardthrone1/Vega-Midas-Lite-Quant-Tower/commit/b44131192c7bad5f8caa5172dd78d5cb7d8a8a60","node_id":"C_kwDOTiNWD9oAKGI0NDEzMTE5MmM3YmFkNWY4Y2FhNTE3MmRkNzhkNWNiN2Q4YThhNjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Hardthrone1/Vega-Midas-Lite-Quant-Tower/commit/aadd5f6e39604f5e7bd636f04cb73b7613cfe780","sha":"aadd5f6e39604f5e7bd636f04cb73b7613cfe780","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Hardthrone1/Vega-Midas-Lite-Quant-Tower/commits/aadd5f6e39604f5e7bd636f04cb73b7613cfe780"}],"sha":"b44131192c7bad5f8caa5172dd78d5cb7d8a8a60","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Hardthrone1/Vega-Midas-Lite-Quant-Tower/commits/b44131192c7bad5f8caa5172dd78d5cb7d8a8a60"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Hardthrone1/Vega-Midas-Lite-Quant-Tower/commits/aadd5f6e39604f5e7bd636f04cb73b7613cfe780/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-26T03:00:29Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-26T03:00:29Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"style(QBT-003): compact debug table — tiny text, short labels\n\nPine exposes no cell padding, so compactness comes from size.tiny on every\ncell plus shortened row labels (Vol ratio -> VolR, ATR ticks -> ATRt,\nConfirmed -> State) and trimmed decimals. Vol basis folded into the Vol row''s\nthird column so the verdict reads first. Last-bar regime label also tiny.\nDisplay only — no classification logic touched, Python port unaffected.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01APBjHWUcg9exofbWm48XK1","tree":{"sha":"a915198698992d64c6b627b913103c33527d0b0b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Hardthrone1/Vega-Midas-Lite-Quant-Tower/git/trees/a915198698992d64c6b627b913103c33527d0b0b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Hardthrone1/Vega-Midas-Lite-Quant-Tower/git/commits/aadd5f6e39604f5e7bd636f04cb73b7613cfe780","verification":{"payload":"tree a915198698992d64c6b627b913103c33527d0b0b\nparent 962ce9fc8fd2c977369f14406253f8ec2ff58f3b\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1785034829 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1785034829 +0000\n\nstyle(QBT-003): compact debug table — tiny text, short labels\n\nPine exposes no cell padding, so compactness comes from size.tiny on every\ncell plus shortened row labels (Vol ratio -> VolR, ATR ticks -> ATRt,\nConfirmed -> State) and trimmed decimals. Vol basis folded into the Vol row''s\nthird column so the verdict reads first. Last-bar regime label also tiny.\nDisplay only — no classification logic touched, Python port unaffected.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01APBjHWUcg9exofbWm48XK1\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQFLJZswV\nf8WkI7MDvjD+nGdZrucpgF4gE8MAougp4KCW7sxgylnOS8k7NhcIxxQSFZ+fEKSAvVtyEvhntj55\niA0=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-26T03:00:32Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Hardthrone1/Vega-Midas-Lite-Quant-Tower/commit/aadd5f6e39604f5e7bd636f04cb73b7613cfe780","node_id":"C_kwDOTiNWD9oAKGFhZGQ1ZjZlMzk2MDRmNWU3YmQ2MzZmMDRjYjczYjc2MTNjZmU3ODA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Hardthrone1/Vega-Midas-Lite-Quant-Tower/commit/962ce9fc8fd2c977369f14406253f8ec2ff58f3b","sha":"962ce9fc8fd2c977369f14406253f8ec2ff58f3b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Hardthrone1/Vega-Midas-Lite-Quant-Tower/commits/962ce9fc8fd2c977369f14406253f8ec2ff58f3b"}],"sha":"aadd5f6e39604f5e7bd636f04cb73b7613cfe780","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Hardthrone1/Vega-Midas-Lite-Quant-Tower/commits/aadd5f6e39604f5e7bd636f04cb73b7613cfe780"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Hardthrone1/Vega-Midas-Lite-Quant-Tower/commits/962ce9fc8fd2c977369f14406253f8ec2ff58f3b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-25T23:58:29Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-25T23:58:29Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"fix(QBT-003): regime filter v3 — fixed thresholds by default, 3 opt-in rules\n\nReverses the v2 adaptive default, which was wrong. Rolling-percentile\nthresholds force a roughly fixed SHARE of bars to read trending regardless\nof what price does, and the cutoff drifts as the window moves: a quiet range\npicked up expansion because its own noise beat the recalibrated volatility\npercentile, and a steady decline lost its trend label because an earlier\nrally had pushed the ER cutoff to ~0.6. Diagnosed by bar-by-bar sampling\nagainst marked chart zones — aggregate coverage/EV statistics, which is all\nv2 was validated on, cannot see this class of error.\n\nv3:\n- Fixed absolute thresholds are the default; adaptive retained but off.\n- Defaults set to the tuned baseline: ER 0.20, ADX 30, vol split 0.95,\n  lengths 5/5/5/40, hysteresis 2.\n- Volatility basis is selectable (Ratio / Absolute / Both / Either). The\n  ratio is self-referential and drifts; the absolute floor is in ticks via\n  syminfo.mintick so it is scale-aware across instruments.\n- Three opt-in rules, all default OFF so the baseline is reproduced exactly:\n  R1 ER shortcut  — catches an impulse before doubly-smoothed ADX ramps\n  R2 chop override— expansion + poor efficiency reads as volatile range even\n                    at high ADX (a wide oscillating channel is not a trend)\n  R3 quiet floor  — absolute ATR below a floor is quiet whatever the ratio says\n- Debug table gains ATR-in-ticks, the vol basis verdict, and a \"rule\" row\n  naming which branch decided the bar, for bar-by-bar sampling.\n- Tick defaults calibrated to measured MGC 5m ATR(5) (17-188 ticks, median\n  51); the first defaults sat below the data minimum and were inert.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01APBjHWUcg9exofbWm48XK1","tree":{"sha":"7a08e6ff7d1e6125b37cd99ad6a89bf0b3024c3c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Hardthrone1/Vega-Midas-Lite-Quant-Tower/git/trees/7a08e6ff7d1e6125b37cd99ad6a89bf0b3024c3c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Hardthrone1/Vega-Midas-Lite-Quant-Tower/git/commits/962ce9fc8fd2c977369f14406253f8ec2ff58f3b","verification":{"payload":"tree 7a08e6ff7d1e6125b37cd99ad6a89bf0b3024c3c\nparent 90cd3bdb69f98e3311012fa21d8a8366c22ce2ee\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1785023909 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1785023909 +0000\n\nfix(QBT-003): regime filter v3 — fixed thresholds by default, 3 opt-in rules\n\nReverses the v2 adaptive default, which was wrong. Rolling-percentile\nthresholds force a roughly fixed SHARE of bars to read trending regardless\nof what price does, and the cutoff drifts as the window moves: a quiet range\npicked up expansion because its own noise beat the recalibrated volatility\npercentile, and a steady decline lost its trend label because an earlier\nrally had pushed the ER cutoff to ~0.6. Diagnosed by bar-by-bar sampling\nagainst marked chart zones — aggregate coverage/EV statistics, which is all\nv2 was validated on, cannot see this class of error.\n\nv3:\n- Fixed absolute thresholds are the default; adaptive retained but off.\n- Defaults set to the tuned baseline: ER 0.20, ADX 30, vol split 0.95,\n  lengths 5/5/5/40, hysteresis 2.\n- Volatility basis is selectable (Ratio / Absolute / Both / Either). The\n  ratio is self-referential and drifts; the absolute floor is in ticks via\n  syminfo.mintick so it is scale-aware across instruments.\n- Three opt-in rules, all default OFF so the baseline is reproduced exactly:\n  R1 ER shortcut  — catches an impulse before doubly-smoothed ADX ramps\n  R2 chop override— expansion + poor efficiency reads as volatile range even\n                    at high ADX (a wide oscillating channel is not a trend)\n  R3 quiet floor  — absolute ATR below a floor is quiet whatever the ratio says\n- Debug table gains ATR-in-ticks, the vol basis verdict, and a \"rule\" row\n  naming which branch decided the bar, for bar-by-bar sampling.\n- Tick defaults calibrated to measured MGC 5m ATR(5) (17-188 ticks, median\n  51); the first defaults sat below the data minimum and were inert.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01APBjHWUcg9exofbWm48XK1\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQL1NlwK0\nfFBiNtUZQrN/gBqAdx/1ZBcfoNtNqzszorvZxhgSFgI4yyfO0gsCKRXvoJjsPMowd7fgJfkYDzJc\nkgg=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-25T23:58:32Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Hardthrone1/Vega-Midas-Lite-Quant-Tower/commit/962ce9fc8fd2c977369f14406253f8ec2ff58f3b","node_id":"C_kwDOTiNWD9oAKDk2MmNlOWZjOGZkMmM5NzczNjlmMTQ0MDYyNTNmOGVjMmZmNThmM2I","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Hardthrone1/Vega-Midas-Lite-Quant-Tower/commit/90cd3bdb69f98e3311012fa21d8a8366c22ce2ee","sha":"90cd3bdb69f98e3311012fa21d8a8366c22ce2ee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Hardthrone1/Vega-Midas-Lite-Quant-Tower/commits/90cd3bdb69f98e3311012fa21d8a8366c22ce2ee"}],"sha":"962ce9fc8fd2c977369f14406253f8ec2ff58f3b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Hardthrone1/Vega-Midas-Lite-Quant-Tower/commits/962ce9fc8fd2c977369f14406253f8ec2ff58f3b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Hardthrone1/Vega-Midas-Lite-Quant-Tower/commits/90cd3bdb69f98e3311012fa21d8a8366c22ce2ee/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-25T09:05:26Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-25T09:05:26Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"fix(QBT-003): regime filter v2 — exhaustive states, adaptive thresholds\n\nThe v1 background froze on stale labels: two disjoint gates (trending\nER>=0.35 & ADX>=20 / ranging ER<=0.20 & ADX<20) left a gap that swallowed\n56.4% of MGC 5m bars as rawState=0, which never confirms. The median bar\nsits squarely in that gap (median ER 0.224, median ADX 22.7), so the two\ngates contradicted each other on the typical bar and the colour kept\npainting the last confirmed regime — up to 4.4 hours at a stretch.\n\nv2:\n- Exhaustive classification: one trend boundary, one volatility boundary.\n  Every ready bar gets a state, so the background always tracks price.\n- Adaptive thresholds by default: each is a rolling percentile of its own\n  indicator (ER p65, ADX p55, vol p50 over 500 bars), so the filter\n  self-calibrates per instrument/timeframe. Fixed mode retained as a toggle.\n- Vol split is a single boundary; the old 0.85/1.15 dead band had dumped\n  every mid-volatility bar into QUIET, inflating that bucket.\n- Debug table now shows each value against the threshold judging it.\n- Regime-change alertcondition; thresholds exported to the data window.\n\nMeasured on MGC 5m: unlabeled bars 56.4% -> 3.4% (warmup only), trend\nshare 58.5% -> 19.8%, ~20 bars per regime block. Re-attributing the\n156-trade parity run with honest labels overturns the earlier read: the\nold RANGING_QUIET headline (+$1557) was 33% freeze artifact. True picture\nis TRENDING_EXPANDING bleeding (-$829, PF 0.56) and RANGING_VOLATILE\ncarrying the edge (+$551, PF 1.18).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01APBjHWUcg9exofbWm48XK1","tree":{"sha":"16842c7629706dc42682700857f71d91b527b0f6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Hardthrone1/Vega-Midas-Lite-Quant-Tower/git/trees/16842c7629706dc42682700857f71d91b527b0f6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Hardthrone1/Vega-Midas-Lite-Quant-Tower/git/commits/90cd3bdb69f98e3311012fa21d8a8366c22ce2ee","verification":{"payload":"tree 16842c7629706dc42682700857f71d91b527b0f6\nparent 1f84b5c406643fe3b423121ade8d9d23d15f209a\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1784970326 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1784970326 +0000\n\nfix(QBT-003): regime filter v2 — exhaustive states, adaptive thresholds\n\nThe v1 background froze on stale labels: two disjoint gates (trending\nER>=0.35 & ADX>=20 / ranging ER<=0.20 & ADX<20) left a gap that swallowed\n56.4% of MGC 5m bars as rawState=0, which never confirms. The median bar\nsits squarely in that gap (median ER 0.224, median ADX 22.7), so the two\ngates contradicted each other on the typical bar and the colour kept\npainting the last confirmed regime — up to 4.4 hours at a stretch.\n\nv2:\n- Exhaustive classification: one trend boundary, one volatility boundary.\n  Every ready bar gets a state, so the background always tracks price.\n- Adaptive thresholds by default: each is a rolling percentile of its own\n  indicator (ER p65, ADX p55, vol p50 over 500 bars), so the filter\n  self-calibrates per instrument/timeframe. Fixed mode retained as a toggle.\n- Vol split is a single boundary; the old 0.85/1.15 dead band had dumped\n  every mid-volatility bar into QUIET, inflating that bucket.\n- Debug table now shows each value against the threshold judging it.\n- Regime-change alertcondition; thresholds exported to the data window.\n\nMeasured on MGC 5m: unlabeled bars 56.4% -> 3.4% (warmup only), trend\nshare 58.5% -> 19.8%, ~20 bars per regime block. Re-attributing the\n156-trade parity run with honest labels overturns the earlier read: the\nold RANGING_QUIET headline (+$1557) was 33% freeze artifact. True picture\nis TRENDING_EXPANDING bleeding (-$829, PF 0.56) and RANGING_VOLATILE\ncarrying the edge (+$551, PF 1.18).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01APBjHWUcg9exofbWm48XK1\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQDhAP5df\nq5WA0GeOFOsL91QQK4UGqppevpyPV6Rdy7sqFhWAYxrqdXuGTtv31y/LNVC6flM8Pfl3sedPL/c9\nwwo=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-25T09:05:28Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"