at the halt bar, any open position is\n    force-closed at that bar''s close (market fill, slippage applied), and\n    equity stays flat to the end (curve flagged halted=True). Trades after\n    the halt no longer exist in results. Truncation is exact because\n    signals don''t depend on equity under fixed sizing.\n  - Zero closed trades no longer false-flags winRateMin/profitFactorMin.\n  - Sharpe returns None below a 1e-12 dispersion epsilon (was ~1e16 on\n    float-noise variance); same guard added to metrics.py Sharpe/Sortino.\n\nParity engine:\n  - Trailing stops implemented: exit.trailing {enabled, mode ticks|points,\n    value, activation}. Arms at activation profit (immediately if absent),\n    ratchets off bar extremes AFTER that bar''s exit checks (stop tested on\n    bar N reflects extremes through N-1 — deterministic, conservative).\n    Trail exits are stop-market: slippage + gap handling apply; the\n    tighter of fixed stop vs trail wins.\n\nTests: risk_test rewritten as 6 hard assertions (per-day limit isolation,\ndaily halt enforcement incl. force-close + flat curve, drawdown halt,\nconsec-loss warn, clean pass, Sharpe None); smoketest gains trailing-stop\ntest #7 (arm/ratchet/exit +$15 and unarmed no-exit). All 13 pass.\n\nReal-data regression (FRD GC/NQ 5m): halts now bind — GC stops at 138\ntrades with dd capped at 10.02% (was 324 trades, 20.7% dd); NQ stops at\n127 (was 438, 35.9% dd).\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RzBdcoGE7AH9tZrWxEsp3w\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ecd049370a2fb0c646f6fd504d29da72e0ecc267","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Hardthrone1/Vega-Midas-Lite-Quant-Tower/git/trees/ecd049370a2fb0c646f6fd504d29da72e0ecc267"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Hardthrone1/Vega-Midas-Lite-Quant-Tower/git/commits/3f8c721b2c7126e578604a3be7f70613d83e4693","verification":{"payload":"tree ecd049370a2fb0c646f6fd504d29da72e0ecc267\nparent c66aa00bdde2a6744b68d8ce41758cea70811951\nau