enson/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stellarshenson/jupyterlab_codex_extension/commits/eeb478bbfc1a28fdf0308f458cdb470f7b8b5d76/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-25T10:55:16Z","email":"konrad.jelen@gmail.com","name":"stellarshenson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-25T10:55:16Z","email":"konrad.jelen@gmail.com","name":"stellarshenson"},"message":"feat: codex cli session management panel\n\nSide panel listing every project used with the Codex CLI, grouped into\nFavourites, Recent and All, with one-click resume, a session switcher,\n`codex fork` branching and trash-aware cleanup.\n\n- server reads `~/.codex/state_<N>.sqlite` read-only with a rollout-JSONL\n  fallback and a migration-head guard, and owns favourites plus the\n  per-project conversation pin in its own sidecar\n- launch argv composed at a single site (`codex`, `codex resume <id>`,\n  `codex fork <id>`, optional `--dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox`)\n  and spawned through a SIGWINCH init waiter that execs codex, so the pid\n  identity survives for terminal reuse\n- terminal reuse keyed per conversation, so a new session followed by a\n  fork cannot start a second codex on a live conversation\n- every destructive path reports what it actually did (`removed_count` /\n  `failed_count`) and names archive-vs-permanent from JupyterLab''s own\n  trash setting; a permanent delete asks twice\n- 84 pytest, 33 jest, 27 Galata tests; acceptance criteria and defects\n  tracked under `docs/`","tree":{"sha":"4ac70a65942ad279e957c9576774690d7eb507f9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stellarshenson/jupyterlab_codex_extension/git/trees/4ac70a65942ad279e957c9576774690d7eb507f9"},"url":"https://api